# Copy to .env.local (git-ignored) and adjust. The Makefile reads it: NAME=value lines, no quotes,
# exported to everything `make` runs.

# The repo `make dev` runs `anfra serve` in: one with Data Apps.
ANFRA_DEV_REPO=../anfra-demo-data

# The cloud server used by the `anfra.ai` choice in `anfra auth login`. Embedded at build time;
# rebuild with make build-dev after changing it. Use the cloud's public origin (Vite in local dev).
# HTTPS is required except on literal 127.0.0.1 or [::1]; localhost is not accepted for HTTP.
# Without this setting, enter an organization URL instead of choosing anfra.ai.
# ANFRA_HOSTED_ORIGIN=http://127.0.0.1:5173

# The sidecars, for an anfra built from source, which embeds none. Unset, make dev runs the releases
# manifest.yml pins, from .sidecars/ (make sidecars). To run your own builds instead: their
# binaries, as absolute paths, since anfra serve runs from inside ANFRA_DEV_REPO ...
# ANFRA_NODE_BIN=
# ANFRA_CANAL_QUERY_BIN=
# ... or long-running ones to dial, so a Go rebuild does not respawn them.
# ANFRA_NODE_URL=
# ANFRA_CANAL_QUERY_URL=
# Run sidecars whose version is not the one manifest.yml pins (scripts/sidecars.sh check refuses).
# ANFRA_SIDECAR_SKIP_VERSION_CHECK=1

# Where make dev's Vite dev server serves the Data App frontend; anfra serve's pages redirect there.
# ANFRA_APPSERVE_DEV_URL=http://127.0.0.1:5173

# Traces from anfra and the anfra-node it spawns, to an OpenTelemetry collector's OTLP/HTTP receiver.
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:4318
